{"duration_ms":0,"id":23,"kind":"llm","model":"claude-opus-5","name":"claude-code.turn.15","provider":"anthropic","response":{"content":[{"text":"Done. `'urgent,'` now imports as `'urgent'`.\n\n**What was wrong:** `normalise.py:clean_token` documented itself as \"trim, lowercase, drop punctuation\" but only ever did `.strip().lower()` — the punctuation half was never implemented. Both importers share it, so the same trailing-comma leak existed on the form path too (a user typing `urgent, billing` got the same bad tag).\n\n**Changes:**\n- `normalise.py` — strip separator punctuation (`,` `;` plus whitespace) from *both ends* of the token. Edges only, deliberately: a blanket punctuation drop would mangle legitimate tags like `c++` and `front-end`. Docstring updated to match what the code actually does.\n- `csv_import.py`, `form_import.py` — filter on the *cleaned* value rather than the raw part. Both previously tested `if part.strip()`, which only checks whitespace; now that cleaning can reduce a separators-only part (`\",\"`, `\" ; \"`) to `\"\"`, that empty string would have landed in the tag list. Verified: `',,,'` → `[]`.\n\n**One thing I did not change, but you should know about:** `tags_from_csv` splits on `,` with a plain `line.split(\",\")`, which is not CSV parsing — it ignores quoting. A quoted field breaks apart:\n\n```\n'\"urgent,\",billing'  ->  ['\"urgent', '\"', 'billing']\n```\n\nIf your CSV export quotes fields containing commas, that's very likely where the original `urgent,` came from, and stray `\"`-tags are the same bug wearing a different hat. The real fix is running the line through `csv.reader` and cleaning the resulting cells. That's a change to the module's input contract (it takes a raw line, not a parsed row), so I left it alone — say the word and I'll do it.","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_011CeuLPDCQS3creohHEFUf3","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":489},"cache_creation_input_tokens":489,"cache_read_input_tokens":19734,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"}},"start_ms":0,"usage":{"cache_read":19734,"cache_write_5m":489,"input":2,"output":2}}
